      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This small discrepancy can be really annoying. I had people complaining to me that stuff in my world is the wrong size, because they set the avatar \"height\" to their real life height but in-game they are 10-20 cm taller because it's the view height, making everything appear smaller for them.\n\nIn the avatar testing world there is a ruler to measure your avatar height and i watched people literally calling the creator of the world stupid because the height was wrong compared to the \"avatar height\" displayed in the menu.\n\nOther conversations i had: Why you so small? \n\nMy avatar is 160 cm. \n\nMine is too? \n\n*awkward looks*\n\n*starts explaining view height*\n\nYou're wrong it says avatar height not view height!\n\n...\n\nI'm tired of explaining to people that the avatar height is the view/eye height. \n\nIt's weird how some simple text can cause chaos, so PLEASE! change it! so it's more accurate.\n\nJust some values i averaged with my friend's avatars.\n\nReal height: 160 cm\n\nEye height: 147 cm\n\nDifference: 13 cm \n\nRH: 180 cm\n\nEH: 165 cm\n\nDif: 15 cm\n\nRH: 200 cm\n\nEH: 183 cm\n\nDif: 17 cm\n\nThe taller the person is the bigger is the difference.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
