      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This misnaming of height is slowing turning into a problem, as more and more users believe they are \"matching their real height\", they also found all the objects scaled too small. This feels like an issue on the map makers' part, when the issue is the misnaming of a feature.\n\nWe are also seeing \"height creep\" similar to what happened to Second Life (where everyone is around 7 to 8 feet tall). As map makers scale up their world to accommodate users with inflated height, users who have properly scaled avatars have to scale themselves up as well. The scaling slowly lose meaning, and it becomes increasingly difficult for map makers to make things \"big\", \"small\" or \"normal sized.\"",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
